### Error Response Cheat Sheet

| Error Type | Action | Limit |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| Simple (typo, import) | Fix immediately | None |
| Integration (API, contract) | Fix → alt approach → research → escalate | 3 attempts |
| Architectural (design wrong) | STOP phase, log, escalate to user | Immediate |

### Resume Checklist (Quick Reference)

When resuming a build session mid-project:

```
□ Read .build-state.json → current phase/step/sub-step
□ Read .conductor-state.json → project context
□ Read BUILD-REPORT.md → deviations and failures so far
□ git status → check for uncommitted changes
□ Verify artifact integrity → every "complete" file exists + non-empty
□ Read current step from PLAN.md (not full plan)
□ Read current section from ARCHITECTURE.md (grep, not full load)
□ Kill any stale dev servers → read devPort from .build-state.json (default 3000), then: lsof -ti:{devPort} | xargs kill -9
□ Continue from exact sub-step in state file
□ PULSE.md section appended (or created if first skill) — see PULSE-PROTOCOL.md
```

### Anti-Patterns (Never Do These)

| Anti-Pattern | Why It's Wrong | Correct Approach |
|-------------|---------------|-----------------|
| Load full ARCHITECTURE.md | Wastes context, violates Execution Contract #9 | Grep for current step's section only |
| Read ahead in PLAN.md | Biases implementation, violates Execution Contract #8 | Current step only |
| Skip verification because "it looks right" | Violates Real-Only Principle | Run the command, paste the output |
| Modify ARCHITECTURE.md | Destroys the forge baseline | Log deviation in BUILD-REPORT.md |
| Self-certify high-risk steps | Violates Patience Protocol | Compliance subagent reviews |
| Summarize command output | Violates Execution Contract #5 | Paste actual output |
| Write file before its imports exist | Breaks verification, violates Execution Contract #3 | Dependency-aware batching |
| Retry unverified pattern 3 times | Wastes attempts on known-uncertain code | Switch to fallback after first failure |
| Start dev server without killing stale ones | Stale .env values cached (Gap 7) | Kill first, then start |
| Force push or amend commits | Destroys session history | New commits only |

### Compliance Timing Quick Reference

| Step Type | When Compliance Runs | Reviewer |
|-----------|---------------------|----------|
| Contract deployment | Immediately after step | Compliance subagent |
| constants.ts / .env generation | Immediately after step | Compliance subagent |
| Steps with real money/keys | Immediately after step | Compliance subagent |
| Forge-flagged decision trees | Immediately after step | Compliance subagent |
| Normal code writing | End of phase | Compliance subagent |
| Normal component creation | End of phase | Compliance subagent |

